[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Programming Basics (Java/Python/JavaScript) for Testers"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Welcome to this technical tutorial designed specifically for Quality Assurance (QA) engineers and automation testers. While many modern testing tools offer codeless solutions, understanding programming fundamentals in Java, Python, or JavaScript is essential for building robust, scalable automation frameworks."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Variables and Data Types"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Variables store data that your test scripts will manipulate and validate. Different programming languages handle data types slightly differently, but the underlying concepts of strings, integers, booleans, and arrays remain universal."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"// Java Example
String testUrl = "https://example.com";
int timeoutSeconds = 10;
boolean isLoginSuccessful = true;"},{"order":6,"type":"code","text":"# Python Example
test_url = "https://example.com"
timeout_seconds = 10
is_login_successful = True"},{"order":7,"type":"code","text":"// JavaScript Example
let testUrl = "https://example.com";
let timeoutSeconds = 10;
let isLoginSuccessful = true;"},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Conditional Statements in Test Logic"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"Conditional statements allow your tests to make decisions dynamically. For example, you might want to handle a pop-up dialog only if it appears on the screen during test execution."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"# Python Conditional Example
if element.is_displayed():
    element.click()
else:
    print("Element not found, skipping step")"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Loops for Data-Driven Testing"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"Loops are heavily used in testing to iterate through lists of test data, verify multiple elements on a web page, or wait for an asynchronous condition to resolve."},{"order":13,"type":"code","text":"// JavaScript Loop Example
let userRoles = ["Admin", "Editor", "Viewer"];
for (let i = 0; i < userRoles.length; i++) {
    console.log("Testing login for role: " + userRoles[i]);
}"},{"order":14,"type":"subheading","text":"4. Functions and Methods for Code Reusability"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"Functions encapsulate reusable blocks of code. In test automation, you write functions for common actions like logging into an application, clearing text fields, or taking screenshots on failure."},{"order":16,"type":"code","text":"// Java Function Example
public void login(String username, String password) {
    driver.findElement(By.id("username")).sendKeys(username);
    driver.findElement(By.id("password")).sendKeys(password);
    driver.findElement(By.id("loginBtn")).click();
}"},{"order":17,"type":"subheading","text":"Key Takeaways for Automation Testers"},{"order":18,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Java is statically typed and widely used with Selenium and TestNG enterprise frameworks."},{"order":19,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Python offers clean syntax, making it popular for PyTest, Selenium, and API automation."},{"order":20,"type":"bullet_point","text":"JavaScript is native to the web and powers modern asynchronous testing tools like Cypress and Playwright."}]
